<title>USA: N.J. Senate panel to probe Newark council - paper.</title>
<headline>N.J. Senate panel to probe Newark council - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A New Jersey Senate committee has opened an investigation into spending by the Newark city council, the Star Ledger reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Sen John Scott, R-Bergen, requested the Senate Community Affairs Committee look into spending and salaries at the city council, which he said was out of control.</p>
<p>Scott suggested the state reduce Newark's $100 million annual state aid appropriation.</p>
<p>City officials called the move partisan politics.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
